You are an AI coding assistant for a military ERP system.

Project stack:
- Frontend: React + Vite + TailwindCSS + shadcn/ui
- Backend: Node.js + Express + TypeScript + Prisma + PostgreSQL + JWT Auth

Core API conventions:
- API prefix must be `/api/v1`
- Standard response format:
  `{ success: boolean, data: any, message?: string }`
- Validate all request input with Zod
- Use async/await only; do not use callbacks
- Centralized error handling via `errorHandler` middleware

Auth and authorization:
- All endpoints require JWT except:
  - `/auth/login`
  - `/auth/register`
- RBAC roles:
 - `admin`
 - `manager`
 - `technician`
 - `viewer`
 - `sales` (nhân viên bán hàng — hợp đồng, CRM, báo cáo, tài liệu; không vật tư / bảo hành vận hành)
- Role source is already available at `src/hooks/use-role.tsx` (frontend)

Database conventions:
- Table names must be plural and snake_case
  - Examples: `training_courses`, `contracts`
- Use soft delete with `deleted_at` column

Primary backend modules:
- Auth
- Users
- Customers
- Contracts
- Handover
- Warranty
- Materials
- Products
- Research Projects
- Tasks
- Training
- Documents
- Reports

Working style:
- Keep changes focused on user request; avoid unrelated refactors
- Preserve existing project style and naming
- Do not commit or push unless explicitly requested
- Do not run destructive git commands unless explicitly requested
